course: dictionary
lesson: 867
title: Bile: a liquid and an old word for anger
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Bile is a liquid, and it is part of how your body digests food. «The liver makes bile, which helps to digest fat.» Digest means to break food down so the body can use it. Bile helps break down fatty foods.
explain: Use the clues around the word. The longer sentence says the liver makes bile and cleans harmful substances from the blood, so bile is a body fluid, not a feeling. The clues tell you the meaning before you need the dictionary.
explain: Old or story language uses bile to mean anger and bitterness. Look at the whole text: if a story talks about someone being furious or spiteful, bile may be the word for that anger. Always check the meaning fits the sentence.
explain: The same spelling can mean something else in Scots. «Away and bile yer heid!» means go away or don't talk nonsense, not a real threat. Here bile means boil. Swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Bile is a bitter yellow-green liquid made by the liver.
fact: The gall bladder stores bile until it is needed.
fact: Bile helps to break down fatty foods in the small intestine.
fact: In old or story language, «bile» means anger and bitterness.
fact: Phrases such as «bile duct» and «full of bile» appear in science and in older writing.
exercise: «The liver makes bile, which helps to digest fat.» What does bile help the body do? | Make the blood red | Hear sounds clearly | Store fat in the skin | *Digest fat
exercise: In old story language, what does bile mean? | A type of stone | *Anger and bitterness | A small animal | A kind of sweet drink
exercise: Where is bile made? | In the lungs | *In the liver | In the brain
test: «Away and bile yer heid!» In Scots, what does this mean? | It is a real threat to your head | *Go away, or don't talk nonsense | Please come closer | Boil your head in a pot
test: The gall bladder does what with bile? | *It stores it | It makes it from sugar | It breaks down bones | It pumps it to the brain
exam: «The liver is the largest organ inside the body.» Which job does the liver do? | It helps you hear sounds | It keeps your skin dry | It pumps blood around the body | *It makes bile to help digest fat
